on my platforms, and it helped me understand the coordinates for my game.

I made clear to AI that i wanted bottles to get deleted once they had reached the bottom of the game
instead of stacking up and blocking sections of my game, and i knew just letting them fall off the game window
wasn't the best idea, therefore i asked it for inspiration on what i should do. It outputted a good idea
that i could use an if statement, and if the bottle falls below y=-16, then they're destroyed. it also
gave me the idea that the player could gain points once the bottles are destroyed, therefore implemented this
as-well.

These ideas and improvements that i got from Ai significantly aided the development of mt game,
as without it my movement wouldn't be as reliable and i wouldn't have a background track to my game, or at least
they would have taken significantly longer to implement then they did alongside the help of Ai



